  "procedure": "Medians recomputed from pass medians of five calibrated batch means; initial=5 whole-variant rotated passes, repeat/final=11 passes with order rotated after every batch, >=10ms calibration. No trimming/filtering and no switch to ratio-of-paired medians for acceptance. Before is freshly compiled 25a2501; retained phases reused same Rust, final phase builds its actual original addon with a clean proof because current chunk allocation changed. Current/no-guard share current native bytes. Source identities, phase-specific native proofs, equivalence and individual mutation results checked. No-guard and legacy graphs are benchmark-only. All four defect inputs must remain native-admitted and fixed guarded must not lose to explicit TS on any measured platform. Fresh PTY records require exact producing/received bytes and emulator parity with actual native reachability. Retain every non-defect control whose guarded median is >10% slower than before, without reclassifying it as a pass.",
